            Pokemon("Pinsir", "Kanto", listOf("bug", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon127, false, "Its strong pincers are powerful enough to crush solid logs. It will grab foes with its pincers and toss them around or tear them in half. It is a highly aggressive Bug-type that often fights with other forest dwellers for territory."),
            Pokemon("Tauros", "Kanto", listOf("fighting", "water"), R.drawable.pokemon128, false, "Once it starts stampeding, it is unable to stop unless it hits something. Its three long tails are used to lash itself into a frenzy. They say a herd of Tauros can flatten anything in their path, leaving destruction in their wake."),
            Pokemon("Magikarp", "Kanto", listOf("water"), R.drawable.pokemon129, false, "A pathetic Pokémon that is only capable of flopping and splashing. Its swimming prowess is not only weak, but it is also easily swept away by currents. Despite its weakness, it is incredibly tenacious and can survive in the foulest of waters, holding onto a secret power."),
            Pokemon("Gyarados", "Kanto", listOf("water", "dark"), R.drawable.pokemon130, false, "Rarely seen in the wild. Huge and vicious, it is capable of destroying entire cities in a rage. It is said that once it appears, it will not stop its rampage until everything around it is destroyed, fueled by its deep-seated anger from its past form."),
            Pokemon("Lapras", "Kanto", listOf("water", "ice"), R.drawable.pokemon131, false, "A gentle POKéMON that enjoys ferrying people across seas. Its high intelligence enables it to understand human speech. Unfortunately, it has been hunted almost to extinction, making it a rare and treasured sight."),
            Pokemon("Ditto", "Kanto", listOf("normal"), R.drawable.pokemon132, false, "It can reconstitute its entire cellular structure to transform into anything it sees. However, when startled, it will quickly revert to its original amorphous blob form. It is often used for breeding due to its unique transformative abilities."),
            Pokemon("Eevee", "Kanto", listOf("normal"), R.drawable.pokemon133, false, "Its genetic makeup is irregular. It has the ability to alter its body structure to adapt to its surroundings, allowing it to evolve into various forms depending on external stimuli. This adaptability makes it a popular choice for trainers seeking specialized Pokémon."),
            Pokemon("Vaporeon", "Kanto", listOf("water"), R.drawable.pokemon134, false, "Its body composition is similar to water molecules, allowing it to melt into water. It can control water at will, and some legends say it can even disappear into mist. It often lives near clean lakes and seas, using its fin-like ears to detect changes in currents."),
            Pokemon("Jolteon", "Kanto", listOf("electric"), R.drawable.pokemon135, false, "Every cell in its body crackles with electricity, allowing it to generate 10,000-volt lightning bolts. Its fur stands on end, creating a cloak of electrically charged needles for defense. It is incredibly fast, capable of moving at the speed of lightning."),
            Pokemon("Flareon", "Kanto", listOf("fire"), R.drawable.pokemon136, false, "It has an internal flame sac that reaches 1,650 degrees Fahrenheit. When it inhales, its body temperature can reach nearly 3,000 degrees, which it then exhales as fire. It stores and expels heat with ease, making its fur extremely hot to the touch."),
            Pokemon("Porygon", "Kanto", listOf("normal"), R.drawable.pokemon137, false, "A POKéMON that consists entirely of programming code. It can freely move in cyberspace. Porygon is the first artificial Pokémon, created by humans, and can revert to data to enter electronic networks."),
            Pokemon("Omanyte", "Kanto", listOf("rock", "water"), R.drawable.pokemon138, false, "A POKéMON that has been revived from an ancient fossil. It swims by wiggling its 10 tentacles. It is believed to have lived in the warm seas of ancient times, hunting for microscopic prey. Its spiraled shell offers good protection."),
            Pokemon("Omastar", "Kanto", listOf("rock", "water"), R.drawable.pokemon139, false, "Its tentacles are so powerful, they can crush its prey before it eats them. Its spiraling shell is very tough, providing excellent protection against attacks. It went extinct because its shell became too heavy to move efficiently, causing it to slow down."),
            Pokemon("Kabuto", "Kanto", listOf("rock", "water"), R.drawable.pokemon140, false, "A POKéMON that was resurrected from a fossil. Kabuto are said to have lived on beaches 300 million years ago, protecting themselves with their hard shells. It can swim through water at very high speeds, using its legs as paddles."),
            Pokemon("Kabutops", "Kanto", listOf("rock", "water"), R.drawable.pokemon141, false, "Its two sharp claws are like swords. It is said that in ancient times, it cut down its prey with a single swing. It was an agile swimmer, rapidly chasing down its prey underwater. It could also walk on land, preying on small land creatures."),
            Pokemon("Aerodactyl", "Kanto", listOf("rock", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon142, false, "This Pokémon is a relic from the age of dinosaurs. It soared through the ancient skies on huge wings, terrorizing its prey with its sharp fangs. It was resurrected from amber and is known for its incredible speed and ferocity in the air."),
            Pokemon("Snorlax", "Kanto", listOf("normal"), R.drawable.pokemon143, false, "It is not satisfied unless it eats over 880 pounds of food every day. After eating, it goes to sleep right away. Its stomach is so strong it can digest any kind of food, even spoiled ones. It is often found blocking paths, completely oblivious to its surroundings."),
            Pokemon("Articuno", "Kanto", listOf("psychic", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon144, false, "A legendary bird POKéMON that can create blizzards by freezing the moisture in the air with its long, shimmering tail. It is said to appear to help lost travelers in icy mountains, guiding them to safety before disappearing into the snow."),
            Pokemon("Zapdos", "Kanto", listOf("fighting", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon145, false, "A legendary bird POKéMON that appears from thunderclouds. It gains power when struck by lightning. Its thunderous cries are said to cause severe thunderstorms and lightning strikes, bringing about powerful electric storms."),
            Pokemon("Moltres", "Kanto", listOf("dark", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon146, false, "One of the legendary bird POKéMON. Its wings are said to be made of flames. When it flaps its wings, they glow brightly and scatter embers, illuminating the night sky like a magnificent sunset. It is said to bring an early spring to freezing lands."),
            Pokemon("Dratini", "Kanto", listOf("dragon"), R.drawable.pokemon147, false, "A legendary POKéMON that is still a myth to most. Its skin is soft and sheds regularly, growing larger and larger as it does. It lives in fast-flowing rivers and lakes, constantly searching for food. It is said to have lived for a long time in pristine waters."),
            Pokemon("Dragonair", "Kanto", listOf("dragon"), R.drawable.pokemon148, false, "It is said that if it is seen, it will bring good weather. Its body gives off a gentle aura. Many people say they have seen it gracefully soaring in the sky above lakes, controlling the weather with its mystical orbs."),
            Pokemon("Dragonite", "Kanto", listOf("dragon", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon149, false, "A kindhearted POKéMON that flies around the world, saving people and POKéMON in distress. Despite its large size, it can fly faster than the speed of sound. It is said to be very intelligent and noble, capable of navigating through the most treacherous storms."),
            Pokemon("Mewtwo", "Kanto", listOf("psychic"), R.drawable.pokemon150, false, "A POKéMON whose genetic code was repeatedly recombined for research. It was created by a scientist after years of horrific gene splicing and DNA engineering experiments. Its cold, glowing eyes strike fear into the hearts of all who behold it, a creature born solely for battle."),
            Pokemon("Mew", "Kanto", listOf("psychic"), R.drawable.pokemon151, false, "So rare that it is still said to be a mirage by many experts. Only a few people have ever seen it. It is said to possess the genetic code of all POKéMON, allowing it to learn and use any move. It is very playful and curious, often appearing before pure-hearted people."),
            Pokemon("Chikorita", "Johto", listOf("grass"), R.drawable.pokemon152, false, "A sweet aroma wafts from the leaf on its head. It is docile and loves to bask in the sunlight. The leaf is also used to sense the humidity and temperature of the air, helping it find optimal growing conditions."),
            Pokemon("Bayleef", "Johto", listOf("grass"), R.drawable.pokemon153, false, "The aroma of the leaves around its neck has a stimulating effect. It has a spicy scent that makes anyone who smells it feel energized. Its neck is tougher than its pre-evolution, and it uses it to headbutt opponents in battle."),
            Pokemon("Meganium", "Johto", listOf("grass"), R.drawable.pokemon154, false, "The aroma of its flower has a soothing effect on people and POKéMON. It can calm any foe or wild Pokémon it encounters. It is said that its breath has the power to revive dead grass and plants, making it a life-giving force in nature."),
            Pokemon("Cyndaquil", "Johto", listOf("fire"), R.drawable.pokemon155, false, "It is timid and always curls itself up into a ball. If startled, the flames on its back flare up instantly. It can protect itself with these flames, but they are still not fully controlled, sometimes burning itself by accident."),
            Pokemon("Quilava", "Johto", listOf("fire"), R.drawable.pokemon156, false, "It can intimidate foes with the heat of its flames, which can reach extremely high temperatures. Its quick movements are augmented by the fire on its back, making it very agile in battle. It can also create a heat haze to hide its movements."),
            Pokemon("Typhlosion", "Johto", listOf("fire", "ghost"), R.drawable.pokemon157, false, "When it is ready to fight, the flames on its back flare up. It uses these fierce flames to create heat shimmers that obscure its movements, making it difficult for opponents to pinpoint its exact location. Its rage can incinerate everything around it."),
            Pokemon("Totodile", "Johto", listOf("water"), R.drawable.pokemon158, false, "Its powerful jaws are able to crush anything. Even though it is small, it is very courageous. It sometimes mistakes people's fingers for food and tries to bite them, so caution is advised. It loves to play in water and chase after moving objects."),
            Pokemon("Croconaw", "Johto", listOf("water"), R.drawable.pokemon159, false, "Once it bites down, it won't let go until it loses its fangs. The new fangs grow back quickly. Its strong jaws are capable of delivering a crushing bite. It is more aggressive than its pre-evolution, constantly seeking out opponents to test its strength."),
            Pokemon("Feraligatr", "Johto", listOf("water"), R.drawable.pokemon160, false, "It opens its huge mouth and intimidates foes with its many fangs. If it attacks, it will swing its heavy body around and thrash its prey with its powerful tail. Its movements are surprisingly quick in water, allowing it to ambush unsuspecting prey."),
            Pokemon("Sentret", "Johto", listOf("normal"), R.drawable.pokemon161, false, "When it becomes separated from its group, it cries loudly. It stands on its tail to see if enemies are nearby. If it spots a foe, it warns others with a shrill cry. They often take turns keeping watch for predators, always alert."),
            Pokemon("Furret", "Johto", listOf("normal"), R.drawable.pokemon162, false, "The mother FURRET wraps its long body around its young to keep them warm. It is very fast and can easily slip into small holes to escape. Its slender body allows it to pursue prey through narrow tunnels with remarkable agility."),
            Pokemon("Hoothoot", "Johto", listOf("normal", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon163, false, "It always stands on one foot. It changes feet so fast, it is hard to see. It keeps accurate track of time by sensing the rotation of the earth, hooting precisely on time every day. It is often used as a clock by trainers."),
            Pokemon("Noctowl", "Johto", listOf("normal", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon164, false, "Its eyes are special. They can see in the dark and are so well developed that it can even spot small prey from miles away. It can rotate its head almost 360 degrees, allowing it to observe its entire surroundings without moving its body."),
            Pokemon("Ledyba", "Johto", listOf("bug", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon165, false, "It is a very timid POKéMON. If it senses danger, it plays dead to trick predators into leaving it alone. It secretes a fluid from its feet that it uses to clean its hands. It gathers in swarms to protect itself."),
            Pokemon("Ledian", "Johto", listOf("bug", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon166, false, "When the weather gets cold, this POKéMON gathers with others and rubs its forelegs together to warm itself. It flies in groups and eats small insects. It's often mistaken for a ladybug in flight, known for its graceful aerial maneuvers."),
            Pokemon("Spinarak", "Johto", listOf("bug", "poison"), R.drawable.pokemon167, false, "It spins a sticky web from its rear to trap prey. It then waits patiently for the prey to get stuck before moving in to attack. The web is also used as a home, meticulously woven with poisonous silk, ensuring no escape for its victims."),
            Pokemon("Ariados", "Johto", listOf("bug", "poison"), R.drawable.pokemon168, false, "It attaches silk to its prey and then waits for the right moment to finish it off. It can also use silk to mark its territory. Each leg has a small hook that allows it to climb any surface, making it an expert ambush predator."),
            Pokemon("Crobat", "Johto", listOf("poison", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon169, false, "Once it has four wings, it can fly faster and more silently than ever before. It silently glides through the night skies, often unnoticed, and can reach speeds of Mach 3. Its enhanced wings allow it to carry heavier loads and travel farther."),
            Pokemon("Chinchou", "Johto", listOf("water", "electric"), R.drawable.pokemon170, false, "Its two antennae glow brightly to lure in prey, which it then shocks. It uses a light-emitting organ to produce electricity. Chinchou lives in the deepest parts of the ocean, where its light is the only source of illumination, attracting both prey and predators."),
            Pokemon("Lanturn", "Johto", listOf("water", "electric"), R.drawable.pokemon171, false, "The light-emitting organ on its head is so bright, it can penetrate the dark depths of the ocean. It uses this light to blind its prey and then swallow them whole. It is nicknamed 'The Deep-Sea Star' for its dazzling light and ability to thrive in extreme pressure."),
            Pokemon("Pichu", "Johto", listOf("electric"), R.drawable.pokemon172, false, "It is still new to storing electricity, so it can accidentally shock itself. When it is excited, it tends to discharge electricity, sometimes startling itself with a small shock. Despite this, it is very playful and curious, always exploring its surroundings."),
            Pokemon("Cleffa", "Johto", listOf("fairy"), R.drawable.pokemon173, false, "When many stars twinkle in the night sky, CLEFFA are said to descend from space on shooting stars. It is an adorable and innocent Pokémon, often found playing at night in quiet fields. Its star-like shape is believed to bring good luck."),
            Pokemon("Igglybuff", "Johto", listOf("normal", "fairy"), R.drawable.pokemon174, false, "Its body is soft and rubbery. When it starts to sing, it can bounce around unpredictably. If it starts crying, it inflates its body and bounces around even more vigorously, making it hard to control. Its singing can soothe other Pokémon."),
            Pokemon("Togepi", "Johto", listOf("fairy"), R.drawable.pokemon175, false, "It is said that a joyful TOGEPI will share its happiness with those it trusts. It collects happiness from others and is said to bring good luck to those who treat it kindly. It is full of cheer and is often seen wiggling its body with joy."),
            Pokemon("Togetic", "Johto", listOf("fairy", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon176, false, "It is said to appear before kindhearted people and shower them with happiness. It will never appear to people who are mean to others. It flutters its wings and sprinkles joy wherever it flies, bringing blessings to those it deems worthy."),
            Pokemon("Natu", "Johto", listOf("psychic", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon177, false, "It has a habit of staring at things with its big eyes. It cannot fly very well, but it can hop around on its short legs. It is said to be able to glimpse the future, often seen meditating atop cacti or rock formations, silently observing."),
            Pokemon("Xatu", "Johto", listOf("psychic", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon178, false, "It stands motionless all day, staring at the sun. Some say it is seeing into the past and the future at the same time. This behavior makes it seem very mysterious and profound to observers, as it quietly processes visions of time."),
            Pokemon("Mareep", "Johto", listOf("electric"), R.drawable.pokemon179, false, "Its fluffy coat of wool is charged with static electricity. The more static electricity that builds up, the more brightly the light on its tail glows. It is often found in grassy fields, where it generates electricity by rubbing its wool together."),
            Pokemon("Flaaffy", "Johto", listOf("electric"), R.drawable.pokemon180, false, "Its fluffy coat of wool stores so much static electricity that it can get a static shock just by touching it. The rubbery skin on its tail acts as an insulator, preventing short circuits. It uses its hooves to stomp the ground, releasing stored electricity."),
            Pokemon("Ampharos", "Johto", listOf("electric", "dragon"), R.drawable.pokemon181, false, "The light from its tail can be seen from space. Sailors once used the light to guide them. It is highly valued for its ability to illuminate even the darkest nights and guide lost travelers, earning it the nickname 'Lighthouse Pokémon.'"),
            Pokemon("Bellossom", "Johto", listOf("grass"), R.drawable.pokemon182, false, "When it dances, its petals rub together and make a pleasant ringing sound. It gathers in sunny places and performs a mysterious dance, especially when the sun is at its peak. It is said to bring good fortune and cheer to those who witness its performance."),
            Pokemon("Marill", "Johto", listOf("water", "fairy"), R.drawable.pokemon183, false, "The tip of its tail is filled with a light, oily substance that keeps it afloat in water. It is always found near clean rivers and ponds. When it swims, only its tail tip is visible, making it hard to spot in the water. It uses its large ears to hear underwater sounds."),
            Pokemon("Azumarill", "Johto", listOf("water", "fairy"), R.drawable.pokemon184, false, "By sensing the movements of water, it can identify its prey and its surroundings. Its large, round body is very buoyant, allowing it to float effortlessly in even the strongest currents. It can also stand on its tail to observe its environment."),
            Pokemon("Sudowoodo", "Johto", listOf("rock"), R.drawable.pokemon185, false, "It is a master of disguise, pretending to be a tree to avoid being attacked. However, it gives itself away by changing its disguise throughout the year. It hates water and avoids rain at all costs, preferring to blend in with rocky landscapes."),
            Pokemon("Politoed", "Johto", listOf("water"), R.drawable.pokemon186, false, "The cries of POLITOED are said to be signals for the season to change. It is always the leader of the POLIWAG and POLIWHIRL groups, using its loud croaks to direct them. Its call is very powerful and can carry for miles across the water."),
            Pokemon("Hoppip", "Johto", listOf("grass", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon187, false, "This POKéMON is so light that it can be carried by a gentle breeze. It will even link leaves with other HOPPIP to keep from being blown away in strong winds. It floats gracefully through the air, absorbing sunlight to grow stronger."),
            Pokemon("Skiploom", "Johto", listOf("grass", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon188, false, "The flower on its head opens and closes with the sun. It uses the sun's energy to grow. It is said that when the weather warms, this Pokémon will float even higher into the sky, riding the gentle updrafts and spreading its spores."),
            Pokemon("Jumpluff", "Johto", listOf("grass", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon189, false, "It drifts around the world on the wind. It releases its spores to propagate its species. Its light body and cotton-like spores allow it to travel great distances in search of warm climates, sometimes even crossing oceans."),
            Pokemon("Aipom", "Johto", listOf("normal"), R.drawable.pokemon190, false, "Its tail is so powerful that it can use it like an arm to hold onto branches and swing through trees. It can also use its tail to manipulate objects, often using it more dexterously than its hands, and even wrap it around food while eating."),
            Pokemon("Sunkern", "Johto", listOf("grass"), R.drawable.pokemon191, false, "It suddenly falls out of the sky into fields and meadows. It is very weak and is said to evolve only with the help of a Sun Stone. It barely moves and survives on morning dew, patiently waiting for the sun's energy."),
            Pokemon("Sunflora", "Johto", listOf("grass"), R.drawable.pokemon192, false, "When the sun rises, it will start to dance and move. It converts sunlight into energy, making it very active during the day. As the sun sets, it becomes still, folding its petals. Its dance is said to bring warmth and joy."),
            Pokemon("Yanma", "Johto", listOf("bug", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon193, false, "It can see 360 degrees around itself. Its eyes are so powerful, it can detect even the slightest movement from any direction. It can hover in place and suddenly dart in any direction, making it an excellent hunter of small insects."),
            Pokemon("Wooper", "Johto", listOf("poison", "ground"), R.drawable.pokemon194, false, "It lives in cold waters and has an extremely cold body. Its body is always covered in a slimy, poisonous film that can numb any attacker. It moves slowly but is always on guard, using its gills to sense changes in water temperature."),
            Pokemon("Quagsire", "Johto", listOf("water", "ground"), R.drawable.pokemon195, false, "It lives in the water and is very docile. If it bumps into something, it rarely notices and just keeps swimming along. It has a perpetual silly grin on its face, leading many to underestimate its surprising strength and resilience."),
            Pokemon("Espeon", "Johto", listOf("psychic"), R.drawable.pokemon196, false, "It can predict its opponent's moves by sensing the air currents. It is extremely loyal to any Trainer it considers worthy. Its psychic powers amplify when it is fully rested, allowing it to communicate telepathically with its trainer."),
            Pokemon("Umbreon", "Johto", listOf("dark"), R.drawable.pokemon197, false, "When exposed to the moon's aura, the rings on its body glow faintly and it gains a mysterious power. It patiently waits for its foes in the darkness before striking with a powerful attack. It is a master of stealth and nocturnal hunting."),
            Pokemon("Murkrow", "Johto", listOf("dark", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon198, false, "It is said that MURKROW guides people to lost items, but it also enjoys playing pranks on them by snatching shiny objects. It is attracted to anything that glitters, often seen pilfering jewelry or coins from unsuspecting travelers."),
            Pokemon("Slowking", "Johto", listOf("poison", "psychic"), R.drawable.pokemon199, false, "Every time the SHELLDER bites down hard on SLOWPOKE's head, the new toxins enter SLOWPOKE's brain and give it a flash of inspiration. It is said to have exceptional intelligence, capable of solving complex problems and giving wise advice."),
            Pokemon("Misdreavus", "Johto", listOf("ghost"), R.drawable.pokemon200, false, "It loves to sneak up on people and give them a fright. It often uses its eerie wail to scare its targets. It feeds on feelings of fear and sadness, making it appear in places where these emotions are strong. It is known for its mischievous nature."),
            Pokemon("Unown", "Johto", listOf("psychic"), R.drawable.pokemon201, false, "Its shape and form are always changing, taking on forms that resemble letters of the alphabet. It is said that UNOWN communicate with each other through telepathy, forming intricate patterns that can alter reality, though their true purpose remains a mystery."),
            Pokemon("Wobbuffet", "Johto", listOf("psychic"), R.drawable.pokemon202, false, "It hates light and loves to live in dark places. It never initiates an attack. When it is attacked, it unleashes a counterattack that doubles the attack it took. It hides its tail, which it protects dearly, as it is its most vulnerable point."),
            Pokemon("Girafarig", "Johto", listOf("normal", "psychic"), R.drawable.pokemon203, false, "Its two heads often think in opposite directions. The tail head, though smaller, is very powerful and can bite. When sensing danger, both heads will produce psychic energy, forming a powerful defensive barrier to protect its body."),
            Pokemon("Pineco", "Johto", listOf("bug"), R.drawable.pokemon204, false, "It hangs from a tree branch with its head facing down, patiently waiting for prey. Its body is covered in a hard shell that protects it from attacks. It explodes if touched or startled, scattering its shell fragments, which are said to be very sharp."),
            Pokemon("Forretress", "Johto", listOf("bug", "steel"), R.drawable.pokemon205, false, "It protects itself by closing its steel shell. The shell is very tough and is riddled with small holes from which it can fire sharp fragments at high speed. It can also open its shell to reveal its body and attack, creating a formidable defense and offense."),
            Pokemon("Dunsparce", "Johto", listOf("normal"), R.drawable.pokemon206, false, "It can dig its way through the ground at a high speed using its tail. It lives deep underground, avoiding conflict. It only surfaces rarely, usually in search of food or if disturbed, making it a very reclusive and elusive Pokémon."),
            Pokemon("Gligar", "Johto", listOf("ground", "flying"), R.drawable.pokemon207, false, "It glides on air currents using its large wings. It then attacks with its large pincers and poisonous stinger. It uses its claws to cling to walls and ceilings, patiently waiting for prey, and often ambushes from above."),
            Pokemon("Steelix", "Johto", listOf("steel", "ground"), R.drawable.pokemon208, false, "Its body is harder than any metal. It can burrow through solid rock at 50 miles per hour, making tunnels beneath the earth. It lives even deeper underground than ONIX and can withstand immense pressure, its body gleaming like polished steel."),
            Pokemon("Snubbull", "Johto", listOf("fairy"), R.drawable.pokemon209, false, "Despite its intimidating appearance, SNUBBULL is a very playful and affectionate Pokémon. It loves to chase after anything that moves and has a surprisingly gentle nature when around people it trusts. Its large fangs are primarily for show."),
            Pokemon("Granbull", "Johto", listOf("fairy"), R.drawable.pokemon210, false, "It is a very timid POKéMON despite its massive jaws. It dislikes fighting but will bite with all its might if it feels truly threatened. Its fangs are heavy, causing its head to droop, but they can deliver a powerful, bone-crushing bite."),
            Pokemon("Qwilfish", "Johto", listOf("dark", "poison"), R.drawable.pokemon211, false, "When it inflates its body, its sharp spikes are exposed. It then attacks by launching these poisonous spikes at foes. It is a highly toxic Pokémon that lives in warm seas, inflating itself to twice its size to deter predators."),
            Pokemon("Scizor", "Johto", listOf("bug", "steel"), R.drawable.pokemon212, false, "Its pincers are as hard as steel and can crush any foe. It can flap its wings to control its body temperature. The more battles it experiences, the more its steel-hard body shines, reflecting its intense training and power."),
            Pokemon("Shuckle", "Johto", listOf("bug", "rock"), R.drawable.pokemon213, false, "It hides inside its shell, storing berries and fermenting them to make a juice. It then sips on this juice, which it can also use to create various potent liquids for defense. Its shell is incredibly durable, able to withstand strong impacts."),
            Pokemon("Heracross", "Johto", listOf("bug", "fighting"), R.drawable.pokemon214, false, "This POKéMON has amazing strength. It can throw foes up to 100 times its own weight. It proudly uses its horn to battle, especially against other Bug-type POKéMON like PINSIR, aiming to hurl them away with its powerful thrusts."),
            Pokemon("Sneasel", "Johto", listOf("fighting", "poison"), R.drawable.pokemon215, false, "A very cunning POKéMON. It steals eggs from other POKéMON nests while its victims are away. Its sharp claws and speed make it an effective hunter, especially in cold environments, where it moves stealthily through snow."),
            Pokemon("Teddiursa", "Johto", listOf("normal"), R.drawable.pokemon216, false, "Before winter comes, TEDDIURSA hides food in various places. It licks honey that is made from its own paws. It has a crescent moon mark on its forehead that glows faintly, and it is known for its sweet and gentle nature."),
            Pokemon("Ursaring", "Johto", listOf("normal"), R.drawable.pokemon217, false, "With its powerful sense of smell, it can locate food hidden deep underground. It marks its territory by scratching large trees. It can stand up and use its claws to fight when threatened, delivering powerful swipes that can fell a small tree."),
